-- water, as a species in its own right, since a solvent is a substance and belongs in the graph as one.
-- Atoms: 0 the oxygen, 1 and 2 the hydrogens. Its symmetries are the two-fold rotation that exchanges the
-- hydrogens, which is proper, and the molecular plane, improper and acting as the identity on the atoms.
-- Its own proton count is one, which is the spectrum of water.
sp-water : Species
sp-water = (3 , cons (nat-xch (cons 1 nil) (cons 2 nil) , srate-flat 12 , true) (cons ((λ x → x) , srate-flat 12 , false) nil) , cons 1 (cons 2 nil))
